    "sma_slope_threshold": -0.001,
    "_comment_backstop": "atr_stop_replaces_hard_stop=true: the ~k*ATR stop is the real risk floor; stop_loss_threshold (-10%) is a catastrophe backstop that effectively never fires behind the fast-exit stack. Behavior-neutral flag that makes the intent explicit and silences the inert-stop warning (bots #231).",
    "_comment_283": "#283: atr_stop_use_hourly_atr sizes the stop from the 1-hour ATR (14 bars ~ 3.5 trading days) instead of the 5-min ATR (~70 min). The old sizing produced a 0.77% stop on NVDA that intraday noise fired and the 2026-09-14 Monday gap walked through for -$902. atr_stop_min_pct floors the stop width at 1.5% as a backstop against implausibly small ATR readings."
  },
